From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:29:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui: keys typed faster than the frames come keep their
 order

Problem: when several keys arrive in one frame (a quick typist on a
  slow machine; the AROS port draws on the CPU), typing on a selected
  cell started the edit with the first character and dropped the rest
  of the frame's events, and the cell editor took Enter, Tab, Escape
  and arrows from anywhere in that frame. "123" then Enter left 1 in
  the cell; "1", Enter, "2" lost the 2; an Escape before the typing
  cancelled it.
Rationale: a frame now takes keyboard events up to the first key that
  is not typing (an editing, moving or function key, a shortcut, a
  clipboard command); the rest wait for the next frame, in order, as
  if typed more slowly. The frame that opens the editor gives it all
  the text typed in it.
Scope: crates/ui-egui (SheetApp::logic, the grid's keyboard input);
  tests in tests/type_to_edit_one_frame.rs.
Upstream-status: candidate; upstream 0.11.1 has the same code.
Verification: 10 of the 12 tests fail without this change (the other
  two cover Shift+Space and an editor already open); all
  gridcraft-ui-egui host tests pass (691).
Removal: when upstream takes it.
